# Vault backtest data cache (parquet, ~50 MB/year — fetched, not committed)
research/backtest-data/

# Node/operator config files that carry LIVE CREDENTIALS in the clear.
# These live outside the tree today, which is NOT protection — nothing stopped
# the next copy from being committed, and the key inventory of 2026-10-08 found
# that exactly that had already happened: SEVEN distinct real `session_key`
# values are in this repo's published history (three of them from a real PRG-3
# ceremony, in docs/path-a-prg3-deploy-log.md). A session key has no expiry and
# no rotation route, so a committed one cannot be revoked — only the next copy
# can be prevented. `setup_multisig_escrow.py` is CODE and stays tracked; the
# patterns below are anchored on the .json data files only.
signers_config.json
signers_config.json.*
beta_entry.json
betaB_entry.json
escrow-testnet.json
escrow-testnet.json.*
multisig_escrow*.json
reserves.env
